WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Let's check out these very Joker wrenches and see what makes them a kind of neat little wrench to have in your toolbox.

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:13.000
You have your ratcheting end right here, so all you have to do is just flip it over to reverse directions on that.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.000
You don't actually have a switch or anything. You just flip the wrench. They're pretty much exactly the same on both sides.

4
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:25.000
The neat part of these, though, is this little plate that they have right here on this end.

5
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:32.000
So what that does, if you look right in here, you can see it blocks four of these little spots.

6
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:39.000
So when you turn your bolt or nut or whatever you're backing out or trying to get started is usually where this shines.

7
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:46.000
You can see it actually sits on there, so the wrench will actually hold your nut or bolt for you.

8
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Usually if you have a nut up in a really tight spot, it can be a real pain.

9
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.000
You end up trying to put your finger behind it, where with this, if you just put it straight in like that, it will go through.

10
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.000
But put it in right there, it will hold it for you while you get it started.

11
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Just a neat little feature.

